### WAF Detection (Response Signature Method)
```python
import requests
url = "https://target.com"
# Normal request
r1 = requests.get(url)
# WAF-triggering request (with attack signature)
r2 = requests.get(url + "/?id=1' OR 1=1--")
# Compare responses
if r1.status_code != r2.status_code or len(r1.text) != len(r2.text):
    print("[!] A WAF may be present")
    print(f"Normal status code: {r1.status_code}, attack status code: {r2.status_code}")
```

### Side-Site Lookup (Reverse Domain by Same IP)
```python
import requests
ip = "1.2.3.4"
# Use chinaz API or other reverse-lookup interfaces
# You can also query crt.sh for certificates on the same IP
r = requests.get(f"https://crt.sh/?q={ip}&output=json")
```

